WEBVTT

1
00:00:27,762 --> 00:00:30,698
Bro, weather app said this
thing is going to be huge, man.

2
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:33,835
And so we're out here
on this tiny little boat?

3
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:35,537
This was your idea.

4
00:00:35,904 --> 00:00:37,672
I know.

5
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:41,643
You know those weather reports
always exaggerate stuff anyway.

6
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:48,516
Hey, let's take a closer look.

7
00:01:00,762 --> 00:01:04,331
Umm... maybe this is
a close enough look.

8
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:10,070
That storm looks like
it's moving pretty fast.

9
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:13,975
The water does
look kinda rough.

10
00:01:14,274 --> 00:01:16,578
Maybe the weather
reports were right.

11
00:01:17,277 --> 00:01:18,780
Is that...

12
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:21,448
Sharks.

13
00:01:21,683 --> 00:01:23,585
And those waves
are coming towards us!

14
00:01:23,851 --> 00:01:25,853
Uh, maybe we should head back.

15
00:01:26,054 --> 00:01:28,422
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

16
00:01:41,903 --> 00:01:42,904
Nathan?

17
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:44,839
Yo, can this thing
go any faster?

18
00:01:45,006 --> 00:01:47,374
It's the fastest
boat on the island!

19
00:01:47,374 --> 00:01:50,011
Come on, hurry! This thing
is almost on top of us!

20
00:01:50,243 --> 00:01:52,847
Hurry!

21
00:01:57,652 --> 00:01:59,419
We gotta go, man,
that thing is getting close!

22
00:01:59,621 --> 00:02:00,088
Come on!

23
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:02,757
It's as fast as it goes!

24
00:02:05,893 --> 00:02:06,794
Great!

25
00:02:06,794 --> 00:02:08,096
What happened?

26
00:02:08,362 --> 00:02:11,365
Why are we slowing down?
The storm is right there, man!

27
00:02:11,799 --> 00:02:14,234
Holy shit.

28
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:17,639
What? What is it?

29
00:02:17,805 --> 00:02:19,206
The engine!

30
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,375
What do you mean, the engine?

31
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:28,215
We gotta go, man.
We gotta go!

32
00:02:28,516 --> 00:02:30,652
Come on!

33
00:02:31,886 --> 00:02:33,387
You gotta get back
in the boat, man.

34
00:02:33,588 --> 00:02:35,288
You gotta get back in the boat!

35
00:02:37,725 --> 00:02:41,129
Xavier! Xavier!

36
00:02:41,729 --> 00:02:43,898
He fell in the water!
He's in the water somewhere!

37
00:02:44,098 --> 00:02:45,133
Xavier!

38
00:02:45,432 --> 00:02:47,702
Brace yourself!
Brace yourself!

39
00:02:48,136 --> 00:02:50,738
Watch out!

40
00:03:49,597 --> 00:03:52,800
All right, here we are, guys.

41
00:03:53,801 --> 00:03:55,536
Sit in the car with him
for another hour?

42
00:03:55,803 --> 00:03:57,972
Does it look a little
different from last year?

43
00:03:58,206 --> 00:03:59,507
I don't think so.

44
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:02,977
Hey, you two,
start lugging.

45
00:04:03,144 --> 00:04:04,746
Mark?

46
00:04:05,079 --> 00:04:06,547
Hey, uh, Will, right?

47
00:04:06,814 --> 00:04:08,082
Yeah, yeah,
good to see you again.

48
00:04:08,216 --> 00:04:08,950
You too.

49
00:04:09,183 --> 00:04:12,186
I couldn't stay away after
such a great vacation last year.

50
00:04:12,419 --> 00:04:13,688
Hey, you remember
my family, right?

51
00:04:13,688 --> 00:04:16,256
My wife, May,
and our son, Aeden?

52
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:17,091
Good to see you.

53
00:04:17,592 --> 00:04:19,292
You remember my
beautiful wife, Sarah?

54
00:04:19,292 --> 00:04:20,228
-Yeah, good to see you again.
-You ,too.

55
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:21,229
And Logan, Brooke.

56
00:04:21,529 --> 00:04:22,597
-Hey guys.
-Hey.

57
00:04:22,897 --> 00:04:24,699
Looking forward
to another barbecue.

58
00:04:25,566 --> 00:04:29,537
Will still claims it's
the best burger he's ever had.

59
00:04:29,537 --> 00:04:30,772
You have to tell
me how you do it.

60
00:04:31,239 --> 00:04:34,041
Oh, yeah, I'm not ready to
give up that secret just yet.

61
00:04:34,041 --> 00:04:36,443
It's so lovely, but
it's probably the only day

62
00:04:36,711 --> 00:04:38,246
we're going to be
able to go to the beach.

63
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:39,747
There's supposed to be a
storm coming in the morning,

64
00:04:39,981 --> 00:04:42,784
though, so we should probably
head to the beach today.

65
00:04:42,784 --> 00:04:45,452
Oh man, I was really hoping
the weather would cooperate.

66
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,354
Well, the worst part of
the storm is projected

67
00:04:47,622 --> 00:04:49,422
to go north, which
should be okay here.

68
00:04:49,724 --> 00:04:51,926
At least that's what
the news is saying.

69
00:04:52,226 --> 00:04:54,996
Still, it's better to enjoy a
sunny day at the beach, right?

70
00:04:54,996 --> 00:04:55,897
Well, then we will definitely

71
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:57,732
make today a beach day,
right kids?

72
00:04:58,032 --> 00:04:59,432
Well, hey, have fun.

73
00:04:59,432 --> 00:05:00,467
We'll see you guys later.

74
00:05:00,802 --> 00:05:02,603
We're off to grab
some fast food burgers

75
00:05:02,837 --> 00:05:04,371
until you grill up
the real ones.

76
00:05:04,639 --> 00:05:06,774
You better watch
this guy's cholesterol.

77
00:05:07,909 --> 00:05:09,442
See ya.

78
00:05:09,677 --> 00:05:11,579
-See you soon, guys.
-See you.

79
00:05:11,813 --> 00:05:14,615
All right,
let the vacation begin.

80
00:05:17,919 --> 00:05:18,886
Here we are.

81
00:05:22,590 --> 00:05:24,025
Well, looks the same
as it did last year.

82
00:05:24,025 --> 00:05:25,059
Yes, it does.

83
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:28,830
I don't know.
Smells kind of funny in here.

84
00:05:29,697 --> 00:05:31,799
Logan, don't start.

85
00:05:31,799 --> 00:05:33,868
Why don't we get settled
and we hit the beach?

86
00:05:34,168 --> 00:05:37,370
The faster we get moving,
the faster I can work on my tan.

87
00:05:39,974 --> 00:05:42,475
Okay.

88
00:07:28,382 --> 00:07:29,784
Awww, is the beach
not your thing?

89
00:07:29,784 --> 00:07:32,420
Oh no, Logan prefers to
be locked in his bedroom

90
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,256
24 hours a day
playing video games.

91
00:07:35,589 --> 00:07:37,191
Video games won't
give me skin cancer.

92
00:07:37,425 --> 00:07:38,292
They will destroy your eyesight.

93
00:07:38,526 --> 00:07:40,428
Mm-hmm.
Teenagers.

94
00:07:40,661 --> 00:07:42,096
Can we go into town?

95
00:07:42,430 --> 00:07:46,233
Not yet. I want you to try to
enjoy the outside, Logan.

96
00:07:49,837 --> 00:07:52,206
Lame.

97
00:07:54,508 --> 00:07:56,043
So, where are you from again?

98
00:07:56,243 --> 00:07:57,745
Right outside of Chicago.

99
00:07:58,112 --> 00:07:59,847
Ah, I went there once.

100
00:07:59,847 --> 00:08:01,983
My dad wanted to go
to a game at Wrigley.

101
00:08:02,283 --> 00:08:03,517
I've never been.

102
00:08:03,517 --> 00:08:04,585
Really?

103
00:08:04,819 --> 00:08:07,188
Yeah, my parents
are White Sox fans.

104
00:08:08,122 --> 00:08:10,257
I'm sorry.

105
00:08:12,259 --> 00:08:14,228
It must be nice living
in a place like this

106
00:08:14,462 --> 00:08:15,997
all year round.

107
00:08:16,230 --> 00:08:17,898
It's all right.

108
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:21,635
You know, it gets
boring after a while, but...

109
00:08:22,536 --> 00:08:24,005
Really?

110
00:08:24,238 --> 00:08:25,139
I mean...

111
00:08:25,439 --> 00:08:26,941
I could never get used to it.

112
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:28,476
The weather is so nice.

113
00:08:28,909 --> 00:08:30,711
The weather is definitely fire.

114
00:08:34,448 --> 00:08:37,818
Hey! You guys want
to head into town?

115
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:41,989
Sure.

116
00:08:47,762 --> 00:08:49,363
So what's it like living
down here all year long?

117
00:08:49,663 --> 00:08:51,165
Do you guys enjoy that?
Yeah, it's great.

118
00:08:51,465 --> 00:08:54,268
I mean, you guys showed up
at kind of an unlucky time.

119
00:08:54,503 --> 00:08:55,436
Oh my gosh.

120
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:57,371
Did you guys see
this about the storm?

121
00:08:57,605 --> 00:08:59,273
It's... it's incredible.

122
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:00,775
I hope everyone's okay.

123
00:09:01,008 --> 00:09:02,676
Yeah, you know,
the reports claimed

124
00:09:02,910 --> 00:09:05,146
at least three
fatalities already.

125
00:09:05,846 --> 00:09:08,315
Fortunately, that was
about 300 miles away.

126
00:09:08,315 --> 00:09:09,250
I did hear the storm was

127
00:09:09,550 --> 00:09:11,218
starting to slow
down a little bit.

128
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,620
Thank God.

129
00:09:12,887 --> 00:09:14,488
Yeah, but the
weather these days?

130
00:09:14,722 --> 00:09:16,857
It just keeps getting
worse and worse.

131
00:09:17,091 --> 00:09:19,060
Thank climate change for that.

132
00:09:19,226 --> 00:09:21,562
I know.

133
00:09:23,397 --> 00:09:25,032
Wow, you're really good.

134
00:09:25,232 --> 00:09:26,734
I've played this game
like a hundred times.

135
00:09:27,034 --> 00:09:29,937
All that dedication is
definitely paying off.

136
00:09:31,639 --> 00:09:33,674
So, have you ever
seen an ocean sunrise?

137
00:09:33,674 --> 00:09:35,209
Not in Chicago.

138
00:09:36,143 --> 00:09:38,012
You and I should
check it out tomorrow.

139
00:09:38,979 --> 00:09:40,147
Yeah.

140
00:09:40,381 --> 00:09:41,415
That would be great.

141
00:09:42,249 --> 00:09:45,753
Um, but the storm, it looks
pretty bad, don't you think?

142
00:09:46,053 --> 00:09:48,689
It'll miss us by
like 50 miles or so.

143
00:09:48,889 --> 00:09:51,659
Might get a little wind.

144
00:09:52,159 --> 00:09:54,295
Okay. What time?

145
00:09:55,429 --> 00:09:56,597
Meet you at, like, 5 a.m.?

146
00:09:56,831 --> 00:09:57,765
If you can get up that early.

147
00:09:57,765 --> 00:09:59,500
I'll be up.

148
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:02,636
You guys?
We're leaving.

149
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:04,972
Um, gotta go.

150
00:10:05,272 --> 00:10:06,474
See you there?

151
00:10:06,474 --> 00:10:08,342
Definitely. 5 a.m.?

152
00:10:08,609 --> 00:10:11,312
See you there.

153
00:10:21,590 --> 00:10:24,125
I'll be in my room.

154
00:10:27,061 --> 00:10:29,797
Would it be okay
if I woke up early

155
00:10:30,064 --> 00:10:33,234
in the morning and went
and saw the sunrise?

156
00:10:33,502 --> 00:10:35,570
Sunrise? You?

157
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:37,138
With who?

158
00:10:37,438 --> 00:10:39,608
With Aeden.

159
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,809
Yeah, I suppose it'd be okay.

160
00:10:41,809 --> 00:10:44,712
I don't think so, Mark.

161
00:10:46,747 --> 00:10:49,150
You don't really know Aeden
that well.

162
00:10:49,683 --> 00:10:50,885
We just hung out.

163
00:10:51,118 --> 00:10:52,720
And you know his parents.

164
00:10:52,953 --> 00:10:55,022
That doesn't mean you know him.

165
00:10:55,923 --> 00:10:57,024
Your mom's right.

166
00:10:57,258 --> 00:10:58,192
Step-mom.

167
00:10:58,459 --> 00:11:02,597
Brooke, we can go together
one morning as a family.

168
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:04,633
-But I don't...
-No buts.

169
00:11:05,099 --> 00:11:06,500
We're not going to
let you off alone

170
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:08,402
with some
boy you barely know.

171
00:11:09,303 --> 00:11:10,337
You heard her.

172
00:11:15,776 --> 00:11:18,145
She's never going to
respect me, is she?

173
00:11:18,145 --> 00:11:20,314
You always let me
be the villain.

174
00:11:21,749 --> 00:11:24,185
[door slams]

175
00:11:27,288 --> 00:11:28,523
[door slams]

176
00:11:28,789 --> 00:11:30,257
There it is.

177
00:11:30,559 --> 00:11:32,960
Let's go.

178
00:11:37,566 --> 00:11:40,100
[screams]

179
00:11:40,434 --> 00:11:42,303
We were supposed to be
on a strict budget and

180
00:11:42,504 --> 00:11:44,506
we already spent too
much money at the arcade.

181
00:11:44,738 --> 00:11:46,240
I just wanted us
to have some fun.

182
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,308
It's vacation.

183
00:11:47,542 --> 00:11:49,243
A vacation that we have
to drive the hatchback to

184
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:51,712
because we couldn't afford
payments on the SUV anymore.

185
00:11:52,012 --> 00:11:53,881
Can we please just
not do this right now?

186
00:11:54,114 --> 00:11:57,484
Can we just enjoy
ourselves while we're here?

187
00:11:57,718 --> 00:12:00,821
I promise you I will deal
with things when we get home.

188
00:12:01,623 --> 00:12:02,691
Sure.

189
00:12:02,923 --> 00:12:04,858
Sorry I said anything.

190
00:12:25,547 --> 00:12:26,814
Come on, hon.

191
00:12:27,147 --> 00:12:28,583
Why don't you go to
bed if you're so tired?

192
00:12:28,816 --> 00:12:30,351
Dad.

193
00:12:30,685 --> 00:12:33,555
Oh boy, sorry,
it's the sun.

194
00:12:33,787 --> 00:12:36,457
Really takes it right
out of you, huh?

195
00:12:37,692 --> 00:12:39,126
Okay.

196
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:40,595
You coming?

197
00:12:40,894 --> 00:12:43,831
You're going to bed?

198
00:12:44,566 --> 00:12:46,433
I suppose so.

199
00:12:49,236 --> 00:12:50,137
All right.

200
00:12:50,437 --> 00:12:52,273
-We're not finished playing.
-Good night.

201
00:12:52,507 --> 00:12:53,407
Play solitaire.

202
00:12:53,708 --> 00:12:56,043
Night.

203
00:13:00,649 --> 00:13:03,484
I'm going to go to bed, too.

204
00:13:03,718 --> 00:13:06,086
What?

205
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:08,455
Why?

206
00:13:08,690 --> 00:13:10,858
Got early morning plans?

207
00:13:12,393 --> 00:13:15,563
No. I guess I'm just
tired from sun, too.

208
00:13:17,732 --> 00:13:19,099
Fine.

209
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,334
I'm on vacation.

210
00:13:20,568 --> 00:13:23,571
And I think I deserve
to have a little bit of fun.

211
00:13:25,205 --> 00:13:27,841
Yeah.

212
00:13:30,044 --> 00:13:33,715
I mean, if I don't
tell Mom and Dad,

213
00:13:33,715 --> 00:13:37,284
what are you going to do for me?

214
00:13:40,622 --> 00:13:43,290
I'll...

215
00:13:43,525 --> 00:13:47,127
I'll buy you that stupid
video game you want. Okay?

216
00:13:47,127 --> 00:13:49,897
-The deluxe version?
-Yeah. Sure. The deluxe version.

217
00:13:49,897 --> 00:13:51,131
Whatever that means.

218
00:13:51,599 --> 00:13:54,736
But wait, what if Mom and Dad
get up before you get back?

219
00:13:54,968 --> 00:13:57,371
Then you better come
up with a good cover.

220
00:14:01,442 --> 00:14:04,445
You get me the video game,
I'll give you an alibi.

221
00:14:04,779 --> 00:14:05,680
Deal?

222
00:14:05,913 --> 00:14:08,215
Deal.

223
00:14:08,482 --> 00:14:11,018
[spits]

224
00:14:28,737 --> 00:14:32,239
-Hey.
-Hey.

225
00:14:32,473 --> 00:14:36,711
-Parents cool with you going?
-Yeah. Totally.

226
00:14:37,010 --> 00:14:39,380
Awesome.

227
00:14:39,614 --> 00:14:42,015
Shall we?

228
00:15:02,903 --> 00:15:04,639
I love the smell of the ocean.

229
00:15:05,239 --> 00:15:09,711
Yeah, it's right over that
hill. Check it out in a minute.

230
00:15:10,077 --> 00:15:12,881
-Yo.
-Yo, Isaac.

231
00:15:13,213 --> 00:15:15,482
This is Brooke.
Brooke, Isaac.

232
00:15:15,817 --> 00:15:17,117
-Hey.
-Hey.

233
00:15:17,117 --> 00:15:18,185
While you guys
have some fun,

234
00:15:18,753 --> 00:15:21,188
I'm going to get some fishin'
in before the rain starts.

235
00:15:21,422 --> 00:15:23,223
Yeah, we're just going
to go check out sun rise.

236
00:15:23,424 --> 00:15:24,826
Try to.

237
00:15:24,826 --> 00:15:25,693
Be my guest.

238
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,428
I'll go back to the truck
and get more beers.

239
00:15:27,662 --> 00:15:29,831
Beers?

240
00:15:30,063 --> 00:15:32,399
Maybe grab some cola, too.

241
00:15:33,033 --> 00:15:34,569
-You got it.
-Okay.

242
00:15:39,674 --> 00:15:42,075
I'm really glad you came.

243
00:15:42,309 --> 00:15:45,547
Yeah, me too.
I definitely needed it.

244
00:15:45,547 --> 00:15:47,782
Want to get away from
your parents, huh?

245
00:15:47,782 --> 00:15:49,551
That and my brother.

246
00:15:49,784 --> 00:15:51,218
I can definitely
understand that.

247
00:15:51,686 --> 00:15:54,556
I'm surprised they
even let you come out.

248
00:15:54,823 --> 00:15:56,089
Yeah, about that.

249
00:15:56,089 --> 00:15:58,025
They didn't know you're here.

250
00:15:59,928 --> 00:16:00,862
I thought I was
the bad influence.

251
00:16:01,094 --> 00:16:03,798
I'm not a bad influence.

252
00:16:04,031 --> 00:16:06,033
I just...

253
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:08,636
There's some weird stuff going
on with my dad and step-mom.

254
00:16:08,636 --> 00:16:09,704
I just need to get away.

255
00:16:09,970 --> 00:16:11,539
Something's going on?

256
00:16:12,941 --> 00:16:15,342
My dad lost his job as a nurse.

257
00:16:16,009 --> 00:16:17,612
-Sorry.
-It's fine. He got a new one.

258
00:16:17,612 --> 00:16:18,713
He's a paramedic.

259
00:16:18,979 --> 00:16:22,416
But it doesn't
exactly pay the same.

260
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:24,384
At all.

261
00:16:24,686 --> 00:16:26,386
So...

262
00:16:26,621 --> 00:16:28,890
All they do is talk about money
all the time.

263
00:16:29,122 --> 00:16:31,826
Like, all the time.

264
00:16:32,125 --> 00:16:34,629
It's just things are...

265
00:16:38,633 --> 00:16:40,802
Well... I'm glad
I could be a distraction.

266
00:16:40,802 --> 00:16:42,770
At least a little bit.

267
00:16:43,905 --> 00:16:46,340
Me too.

268
00:16:48,810 --> 00:16:51,345
Nice view.

269
00:16:51,713 --> 00:16:52,547
Yeah.

270
00:16:52,814 --> 00:16:55,115
Maybe we'll catch the
sunrise another day.

271
00:16:56,383 --> 00:17:00,354
Do you always bring
out-of-towners up here?

272
00:17:00,555 --> 00:17:01,623
No.

273
00:17:01,890 --> 00:17:04,491
Just you.

274
00:17:08,061 --> 00:17:08,830
[thunder]

275
00:17:09,129 --> 00:17:11,633
Whoa!
That was really loud.

276
00:17:11,966 --> 00:17:12,600
Should we go?

277
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,100
Yo, Isaac.

278
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:14,903
What's up?

279
00:17:15,503 --> 00:17:18,540
The storm's path is changing.
A surge is coming.

280
00:17:19,273 --> 00:17:20,542
We should get off the beach.

281
00:17:20,775 --> 00:17:22,209
I thought you said
it wouldn't get this bad.

282
00:17:22,544 --> 00:17:24,546
Sometimes weather
has a mind of its own.

283
00:17:25,112 --> 00:17:25,780
We should get out of here.

284
00:17:26,014 --> 00:17:27,247
And go where?

285
00:17:27,481 --> 00:17:28,650
Into town.

286
00:17:28,917 --> 00:17:31,351
Come on.

287
00:17:54,909 --> 00:17:56,778
It's really raining.

288
00:17:57,210 --> 00:17:58,513
The storm.

289
00:17:58,813 --> 00:18:01,081
I guess it didn't
miss us like they said.

290
00:18:01,315 --> 00:18:04,151
We should find cover.

291
00:18:04,652 --> 00:18:06,754
We can wait it out 'til
the rain lets up.

292
00:18:07,555 --> 00:18:09,891
No, what about the surge
that Isaac mentioned?

293
00:18:09,891 --> 00:18:10,992
It'll be fine.

294
00:18:11,291 --> 00:18:13,795
You don't want to be
on the beach in a surge.

295
00:18:28,943 --> 00:18:30,078
What's going on?

296
00:18:30,078 --> 00:18:32,847
I don't know.

297
00:18:33,313 --> 00:18:34,816
Oh my God, I thought
the worst of the storm

298
00:18:35,049 --> 00:18:36,249
was supposed to pass us.

299
00:18:36,249 --> 00:18:37,284
I don't know.

300
00:18:37,752 --> 00:18:39,219
These storms have been known
to turn on a dime

301
00:18:39,486 --> 00:18:41,388
more and more often these days.

302
00:18:45,727 --> 00:18:47,862
Where's Brooke?

303
00:18:49,831 --> 00:18:52,232
Brooke?

304
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,769
Brooke!

305
00:18:59,674 --> 00:19:01,208
She's gone.

306
00:19:01,509 --> 00:19:03,645
What?

307
00:19:03,911 --> 00:19:05,847
Logan...

308
00:19:06,146 --> 00:19:07,682
Where's your sister?

309
00:19:10,718 --> 00:19:12,887
Logan.

310
00:19:15,056 --> 00:19:16,124
Come on.

311
00:19:16,356 --> 00:19:19,794
How dangerous would
the beach be right now?

312
00:19:20,061 --> 00:19:22,563
Please do not tell me that
she snuck out this morning.

313
00:19:22,797 --> 00:19:26,166
Well, I'm sorry,
she wanted to go.

314
00:19:26,834 --> 00:19:27,735
She told me she'd buy me a

315
00:19:27,735 --> 00:19:28,903
video game if I didn't
say anything.

316
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:30,303
A video game?

317
00:19:30,538 --> 00:19:31,338
She's at the beach.
She's at the beach.

318
00:19:31,338 --> 00:19:32,573
Damn it, Logan!

319
00:19:32,807 --> 00:19:34,142
Why didn't you tell us
the moment she left?

320
00:19:34,374 --> 00:19:36,911
I was asleep when she left!

321
00:19:37,177 --> 00:19:38,245
She just told me last night!

322
00:19:38,579 --> 00:19:40,615
Well, then you should
have told us last night.

323
00:19:40,915 --> 00:19:43,183
Correct.
Call her.

324
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:51,458
This is Brooke,
please leave a message.

325
00:19:51,693 --> 00:19:52,994
Brooke, Brooke, honey,
please call us back

326
00:19:53,193 --> 00:19:54,461
and let us
know where you are.

327
00:19:54,696 --> 00:19:57,732
We're not mad.
We're just worried.

328
00:19:58,498 --> 00:19:59,567
-Straight to voicemail.
-Great.

329
00:19:59,867 --> 00:20:02,235
[knocking]

330
00:20:05,006 --> 00:20:06,541
Is Aeden here?

331
00:20:10,011 --> 00:20:10,778
We told him last night

332
00:20:11,211 --> 00:20:12,379
he couldn't go because
of the weather.

333
00:20:12,647 --> 00:20:14,281
We told Brooke that
she couldn't go either.

334
00:20:14,549 --> 00:20:16,416
We need to find them.

335
00:20:16,918 --> 00:20:19,252
What? Out there?

336
00:20:19,486 --> 00:20:21,221
Yeah, before it gets worse.

337
00:20:21,522 --> 00:20:24,125
The first part of the storm
usually isn't the most severe.

338
00:20:24,125 --> 00:20:24,792
-No!
-Logan, not now.

339
00:20:24,792 --> 00:20:25,860
Why?

340
00:20:26,094 --> 00:20:27,795
Because your sister
is out there, that's why.

341
00:20:27,795 --> 00:20:29,063
Well, her and Aeden are probably
in a building or something.

342
00:20:29,329 --> 00:20:30,865
Well, you don't know that.

343
00:20:31,132 --> 00:20:33,201
Listen to me. Storm or not,
we are going out there

344
00:20:33,201 --> 00:20:34,068
to find them.

345
00:20:34,802 --> 00:20:36,771
If the storm is severe enough
to have caused a surge,

346
00:20:37,004 --> 00:20:40,641
we need to find Aeden and Brooke
before the next surge hits.

347
00:20:40,942 --> 00:20:43,211
That's when flooding
will be at its worst.

348
00:20:43,376 --> 00:20:45,412
How bad are we talking, here?

349
00:20:45,412 --> 00:20:46,614
This town is in a basin,

350
00:20:46,814 --> 00:20:48,549
and tends to fill with
water in a storm.

351
00:20:48,883 --> 00:20:52,419
Highest on record was six feet,
but that was before my time.

352
00:20:52,687 --> 00:20:55,556
Either way, the beach isn't
safe at all right now.

353
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:58,960
Even if the storm bypasses us,
the surges are way too severe.

354
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,427
Okay.

355
00:21:00,695 --> 00:21:03,363
Babe, you stay here with Logan
in case Brooke and Aeden come.

356
00:21:03,363 --> 00:21:06,333
-But Dad!
-Logan, no buts!

357
00:21:06,567 --> 00:21:08,335
You should have told us.

358
00:21:09,237 --> 00:21:10,238
Let's go.

359
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:12,573
We'll be back.

360
00:21:12,874 --> 00:21:14,474
We'll be right back.

361
00:21:24,484 --> 00:21:28,488
Will it ever stop raining?

362
00:21:29,891 --> 00:21:31,291
Aeden?

363
00:21:31,592 --> 00:21:34,562
We need... we need
to move further inland.

364
00:21:37,497 --> 00:21:40,067
Has it ever been
this high up before?

365
00:21:42,069 --> 00:21:43,571
It'll stop soon.

366
00:21:51,078 --> 00:21:52,980
It's so cold.

367
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:54,215
At least it's morning.

368
00:21:54,749 --> 00:21:58,418
So the lights being out
won't be as big a deal.

369
00:21:59,954 --> 00:22:02,322
The surge has already
taken over the whole town.

370
00:22:02,957 --> 00:22:04,592
So we can't outrun it.

371
00:22:04,592 --> 00:22:05,827
There's no telling what
kind of debris

372
00:22:05,827 --> 00:22:07,628
could already
be in the water.

373
00:22:11,331 --> 00:22:13,668
There!

374
00:22:14,502 --> 00:22:16,637
The ladder?

375
00:22:16,871 --> 00:22:18,306
It only takes
like six inches of water

376
00:22:18,506 --> 00:22:20,141
to sweep someone off their feet.

377
00:22:20,373 --> 00:22:21,976
And with how fast it's moving...

378
00:22:23,644 --> 00:22:27,081
No, can't we just like hide
in a store or something?

379
00:22:27,782 --> 00:22:29,449
They're all still closed.

380
00:22:29,449 --> 00:22:31,519
And the water's
rising too quick.

381
00:22:32,153 --> 00:22:33,754
We need to get above it.

382
00:22:34,822 --> 00:22:36,791
Coral Bay sits in a basin,
so it floods easy.

383
00:22:36,791 --> 00:22:40,828
The first floor of these places
will be flooded in no time.

384
00:22:41,062 --> 00:22:42,663
We'll be fine.

385
00:22:42,964 --> 00:22:46,734
We need to keep climbing
and wait for the rain to recede.

386
00:22:48,169 --> 00:22:50,571
Come on.

387
00:22:53,274 --> 00:22:54,474
You go first.

388
00:23:04,619 --> 00:23:06,453
You're doing great.

389
00:23:11,292 --> 00:23:12,459
Gah!

390
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:14,729
Aeden, are you okay?

391
00:23:15,029 --> 00:23:18,766
I'm fine! Go!

392
00:23:51,999 --> 00:23:54,969
And a tropical storm warning
is in effect until 8pm.

393
00:23:54,969 --> 00:23:56,804
Authorities are urging
people to find shelter

394
00:23:57,104 --> 00:23:59,073
and stay off the streets as
the worst part of the storm,

395
00:23:59,273 --> 00:24:01,609
as well as a second surge
with potentially even more

396
00:24:01,809 --> 00:24:04,278
catastrophic flooding
won't hit for a few more hours.

397
00:24:04,578 --> 00:24:06,647
That's not good.

398
00:24:07,581 --> 00:24:09,550
I cannot believe
they went out in this.

399
00:24:09,917 --> 00:24:12,753
Brooke usually doesn't
do things like this.

400
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:15,856
I don't know, maybe
she's acting out because,

401
00:24:16,123 --> 00:24:19,093
honestly, things haven't
been going so great at home.

402
00:24:19,393 --> 00:24:20,761
Especially...

403
00:24:20,995 --> 00:24:23,197
Aeden is usually
more responsible.

404
00:24:23,496 --> 00:24:25,733
Where on the beach
did you say they are?

405
00:24:25,900 --> 00:24:26,534
Uh...

406
00:24:26,834 --> 00:24:28,202
Up here, take a left!

407
00:24:29,236 --> 00:24:32,773
You can't be serious when
you say that this is normal.

408
00:24:33,708 --> 00:24:36,644
No. It's not.

409
00:24:38,112 --> 00:24:39,714
So what do we do?

410
00:24:42,550 --> 00:24:43,751
I don't know.

411
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:48,089
I really hope
my family's okay.

412
00:24:48,522 --> 00:24:49,423
My family will help them.

413
00:24:49,423 --> 00:24:51,559
They'll know what to do.

414
00:24:52,059 --> 00:24:53,327
Our houses are
further from the beach,

415
00:24:53,561 --> 00:24:55,896
so the water won't
be as high there,

416
00:24:56,163 --> 00:24:58,632
if it even manages
to get over the seawall.

417
00:25:06,574 --> 00:25:08,242
There's something out there.

418
00:25:09,844 --> 00:25:10,978
That's my friend!

419
00:25:11,212 --> 00:25:13,314
Isaac! Isaac!

420
00:25:13,547 --> 00:25:14,315
Isaac, hey!

421
00:25:14,315 --> 00:25:15,249
Hey! Hey, Isaac!

422
00:25:15,516 --> 00:25:17,485
-Isaac, up here! Isaac!
-Isaac!

423
00:25:17,718 --> 00:25:19,887
Isaac, get to the ladder!

424
00:25:20,154 --> 00:25:21,322
Aeden!

425
00:25:21,622 --> 00:25:22,890
-Isaac, get up here!
-Isaac!

426
00:25:23,157 --> 00:25:24,125
Isaac, come here!

427
00:25:24,392 --> 00:25:26,027
Come on, get to the ladder!

428
00:25:28,662 --> 00:25:30,164
Isaac, come on! Hurry!

429
00:25:30,464 --> 00:25:32,900
I'm coming!

430
00:25:34,168 --> 00:25:35,269
Isaac, hurry!

431
00:25:35,469 --> 00:25:37,538
Isaac, hurry up!

432
00:25:38,105 --> 00:25:39,807
Ah!

433
00:25:40,041 --> 00:25:40,741
[screams]

434
00:25:41,042 --> 00:25:42,511
Isaac!

435
00:25:42,743 --> 00:25:45,379
No! No! No!

436
00:25:45,613 --> 00:25:48,149
No...

437
00:25:53,888 --> 00:25:55,389
You know, I really
think we should start

438
00:25:55,689 --> 00:25:57,892
preparing in case
we have to evacuate.

439
00:25:58,492 --> 00:25:59,693
Evacuate?

440
00:25:59,927 --> 00:26:02,163
Yeah, let's get some bottles
of water together,

441
00:26:02,396 --> 00:26:03,764
some non-perishables,

442
00:26:04,198 --> 00:26:06,333
and oh, if you have
a first aid kit.

443
00:26:07,935 --> 00:26:10,971
You know, if the news
had said that it was

444
00:26:11,172 --> 00:26:14,842
going to be this awful,
I could have prepared better.

445
00:26:15,142 --> 00:26:17,311
I have a ton of
sandbags in the garage.

446
00:26:17,546 --> 00:26:22,183
I mean, storms
have come through here.

447
00:26:22,450 --> 00:26:25,086
Bad storms,
but this is just...

448
00:26:25,352 --> 00:26:26,620
Insane.

449
00:26:26,854 --> 00:26:30,357
Yeah... yeah.

450
00:26:32,860 --> 00:26:34,795
What is that?

451
00:26:37,865 --> 00:26:40,301
Is that water?

452
00:26:45,673 --> 00:26:48,109
Did you see him?

453
00:26:50,545 --> 00:26:51,812
-Did you think it was a--
-No!

454
00:26:52,113 --> 00:26:54,115
No way!

455
00:26:54,348 --> 00:26:55,716
We didn't see any blood.

456
00:26:56,817 --> 00:26:58,986
He's probably just got
carried away with the current.

457
00:26:59,220 --> 00:27:02,723
He's a good swimmer.
He'll be fine.

458
00:27:03,958 --> 00:27:05,793
We need to get off this roof.

459
00:27:06,293 --> 00:27:06,927
And go where?

460
00:27:07,394 --> 00:27:08,329
Because I'm not getting
back in that water.

461
00:27:08,329 --> 00:27:08,963
I don't know.

462
00:27:09,663 --> 00:27:10,998
Not with what just
happened to Isaac!

463
00:27:11,265 --> 00:27:13,367
I don't know, okay?

464
00:27:13,602 --> 00:27:14,869
We can't stay here.

465
00:27:15,236 --> 00:27:16,937
It's not safe.

466
00:27:16,937 --> 00:27:18,906
We could get stuck by lightning.

467
00:27:26,313 --> 00:27:28,716
How much further?

468
00:27:28,983 --> 00:27:30,084
About two blocks.

469
00:27:30,317 --> 00:27:31,952
Are you sure?

470
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:36,690
Yeah.
I mean, the beach was here.

471
00:27:39,727 --> 00:27:42,163
Could never imagine
a storm surge this deep.

472
00:27:42,463 --> 00:27:45,634
I can't believe the surge
can get worse than this.

473
00:27:46,133 --> 00:27:48,335
I hope the kids find
someplace safe.

474
00:27:49,103 --> 00:27:49,837
Brooke!

475
00:27:50,104 --> 00:27:53,174
Aeden!

476
00:28:00,848 --> 00:28:05,286
-Brooke!
-Aeden!

477
00:28:05,753 --> 00:28:08,189
Do you hear that?

478
00:28:08,389 --> 00:28:12,826
-Brooke!
-Aeden!

479
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:15,429
-Dad?
-Dad?

480
00:28:15,696 --> 00:28:17,666
-Dad! Dad, we're up here!
-Dad!

481
00:28:17,898 --> 00:28:20,868
Up here! Dad!
Dad, come on!

482
00:28:21,135 --> 00:28:23,370
Brooke!

483
00:28:24,905 --> 00:28:27,408
-Brooke!
-Where are they?

484
00:28:27,775 --> 00:28:28,610
Brooke!

485
00:28:28,842 --> 00:28:30,077
-Aeden!
-Dad!

486
00:28:30,344 --> 00:28:31,212
There!

487
00:28:31,478 --> 00:28:34,315
Dad, up here!
Dad!

488
00:28:34,583 --> 00:28:35,517
Thank you, thank you.

489
00:28:35,517 --> 00:28:36,450
We're coming, Aeden!

490
00:28:36,717 --> 00:28:38,485
Brooke, Brooke,
stay there, baby!

491
00:28:41,822 --> 00:28:44,258
Come on.

492
00:28:46,126 --> 00:28:48,329
-No, Dad!
-Dad! Shark!

493
00:28:48,597 --> 00:28:49,797
Get out of the water!

494
00:28:50,030 --> 00:28:52,667
Dad, there's sharks!
Sharks in the water!

495
00:28:52,900 --> 00:28:55,002
Brooke, stay there, baby!

496
00:28:55,302 --> 00:28:57,539
We're coming!

497
00:28:57,771 --> 00:28:59,473
Dad, get out of the water!

498
00:28:59,708 --> 00:29:02,176
Dad, there's sharks
in the water!

499
00:29:02,409 --> 00:29:03,477
Watch out, sharks!

500
00:29:03,777 --> 00:29:04,812
-What did she say?
-What's she saying?

501
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:06,480
I can't hear what
they're saying!

502
00:29:06,715 --> 00:29:07,848
-Sharks in the water!
-I don't know.

503
00:29:08,148 --> 00:29:10,451
-Dad, come on!
-Sharks in the water!

504
00:29:10,685 --> 00:29:13,487
Dad!
Get out of the water! Dad!

505
00:29:13,787 --> 00:29:16,390
What's he say?

506
00:29:16,757 --> 00:29:19,260
Sharks?

507
00:29:22,463 --> 00:29:23,531
What?

508
00:29:23,764 --> 00:29:27,468
Don't move.

509
00:29:28,570 --> 00:29:30,204
Move, come on!

510
00:29:30,437 --> 00:29:31,606
Dad, be careful!

511
00:29:31,839 --> 00:29:33,073
-Get out of the water!
-Dad, come on!

512
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:35,744
Get out of the water!
There's sharks!

513
00:29:36,043 --> 00:29:37,911
Jesus, what do we do?

514
00:29:37,911 --> 00:29:40,515
We need to get out of the water.

515
00:29:42,449 --> 00:29:44,218
But where?

516
00:29:44,451 --> 00:29:46,253
There!

517
00:29:46,487 --> 00:29:48,055
Not too fast, but move!

518
00:29:48,623 --> 00:29:50,157
We do't want to draw attention!

519
00:29:50,759 --> 00:29:52,259
Come on!

520
00:29:52,493 --> 00:29:54,395
Dad, look out!

521
00:29:54,629 --> 00:29:55,963
Dad, help!

522
00:29:56,263 --> 00:29:59,867
Dad, don't go,
there's sharks!

523
00:30:00,234 --> 00:30:01,536
Okay.

524
00:30:01,770 --> 00:30:04,838
Move slowly.

525
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,308
Slow movements, Will.

526
00:30:07,575 --> 00:30:11,412
-Dad, come on!
-Be careful!

527
00:30:14,649 --> 00:30:16,116
[grunts]

528
00:30:16,350 --> 00:30:18,620
Will, come on, man!
Keep going!

529
00:30:18,852 --> 00:30:20,321
You're almost there!

530
00:30:20,555 --> 00:30:22,890
Okay.

531
00:30:24,158 --> 00:30:26,427
I got you, bro, swim!

532
00:30:26,728 --> 00:30:28,395
Swim!

533
00:30:28,630 --> 00:30:29,897
