across that water fast.

795
00:44:21,795 --> 00:44:23,731
We can't jump off into the water

796
00:44:23,964 --> 00:44:25,666
from here because
of all the debris.

797
00:44:26,100 --> 00:44:28,936
We need to find a
way down a floor or two

798
00:44:29,170 --> 00:44:31,606
and climb out a window
into the water.

799
00:44:31,606 --> 00:44:32,907
Then we can maybe
use the debris

800
00:44:33,140 --> 00:44:35,442
as rafts to get
to the marina.

801
00:44:35,442 --> 00:44:36,277
Does that sound good?

802
00:44:36,545 --> 00:44:38,479
Yeah, sounds like a plan.

803
00:44:38,712 --> 00:44:40,414
But if it isn't the sharks,

804
00:44:40,681 --> 00:44:42,651
gotta watch out
for downed power lines.

805
00:44:42,883 --> 00:44:44,519
That electricity goes
through saltwater

806
00:44:44,752 --> 00:44:45,886
faster than fresh water.

807
00:44:46,187 --> 00:44:48,255
Thanks for the fun fact, Ray.

808
00:44:48,489 --> 00:44:50,958
Any time.

809
00:44:51,225 --> 00:44:52,426
Let's go.

810
00:44:52,726 --> 00:44:54,828
There's a door over there.

811
00:45:03,270 --> 00:45:04,539
Easy.

812
00:45:04,805 --> 00:45:07,841
-I can't see.
-Just follow me.

813
00:45:08,209 --> 00:45:10,978
-You okay?
-Yeah. Never better, Ray.

814
00:45:12,079 --> 00:45:15,783
We need to hurry or this place
is gonna collapse on top of us!

815
00:45:18,485 --> 00:45:19,920
Okay. This will do.

816
00:45:20,287 --> 00:45:23,324
I'll go out first and
I'll stop some debris.

817
00:45:23,857 --> 00:45:26,260
Then we can use that
to float to the harbor.

818
00:45:28,630 --> 00:45:31,131
Careful.

819
00:45:38,305 --> 00:45:39,006
Okay, come on.

820
00:45:39,006 --> 00:45:40,642
Hurry, Aeden.
Brooke.

821
00:45:40,874 --> 00:45:44,111
Okay, Aeden. You all right?
You're doing okay.

822
00:45:44,378 --> 00:45:45,479
All right, we got this.

823
00:45:45,779 --> 00:45:47,582
Aeden, come on.

824
00:45:47,915 --> 00:45:49,483
Let's go.
Aeden, grab onto this.

825
00:45:49,750 --> 00:45:52,253
Come on!

826
00:45:56,658 --> 00:45:58,259
It's coming down.

827
00:45:58,492 --> 00:46:01,061
Ray.

828
00:46:04,865 --> 00:46:07,636
Come on, Ray.
The building's coming down.

829
00:46:08,302 --> 00:46:09,604
-Hurry up!
-Come on, Ray! Hurry!

830
00:46:09,903 --> 00:46:12,940
Come on!

831
00:46:14,174 --> 00:46:15,809
Ray!

832
00:46:16,043 --> 00:46:17,144
Let's go.
We gotta go.

833
00:46:17,378 --> 00:46:19,813
Get out here.

834
00:46:20,515 --> 00:46:23,183
We gotta paddle, let's go.

835
00:46:37,632 --> 00:46:40,801
Mom! Mom!
Where's Brooke?

836
00:46:41,035 --> 00:46:44,238
We're gonna find her and
your father. Don't worry.

837
00:46:47,341 --> 00:46:49,577
Come on.

838
00:46:52,614 --> 00:46:55,082
[shouts]

839
00:46:58,687 --> 00:47:00,321
Keep going.
You got this.

840
00:47:07,895 --> 00:47:09,229
Hey, Mom.
There's a cop!

841
00:47:09,531 --> 00:47:11,999
There's a cop!
Maybe Brooke will be with them!

842
00:47:13,601 --> 00:47:16,036
Yeah, maybe.

843
00:47:16,337 --> 00:47:18,872
Come on!

844
00:47:22,777 --> 00:47:27,147
Mom!
Mom, the water! The water!

845
00:47:30,552 --> 00:47:33,354
Babe, come on!

846
00:47:46,967 --> 00:47:49,436
Hang on!

847
00:47:52,574 --> 00:47:55,075
[shouts]

848
00:48:02,216 --> 00:48:04,451
Mom!

849
00:48:05,687 --> 00:48:06,954
We have to get out of the water!

850
00:48:07,221 --> 00:48:08,989
Over here!
Over here!

851
00:48:10,825 --> 00:48:13,427
Go! There!

852
00:48:15,462 --> 00:48:16,598
Come on, come on!

853
00:48:25,540 --> 00:48:27,975
Give me your hand!

854
00:48:39,153 --> 00:48:42,356
Watch it! Watch it!
Move!

855
00:48:45,225 --> 00:48:48,162
Move, move, move!
Give me your hand!

856
00:48:50,765 --> 00:48:51,999
Are you all right?

857
00:48:52,166 --> 00:48:54,234
-I think so.
-I'll tell you what.

858
00:48:54,501 --> 00:48:56,771
The goddamn water's infested
with those damn things.

859
00:48:57,104 --> 00:49:00,675
I'll tell you what.
Blood, and all that debris.

860
00:49:00,842 --> 00:49:02,376
That's attracting 'em.

861
00:49:02,376 --> 00:49:04,378
Right now, outside, there's
nothing more than just a...

862
00:49:04,378 --> 00:49:08,248
a big... death pit.
I'm telling you.

863
00:49:11,686 --> 00:49:14,656
[screams]

864
00:49:27,702 --> 00:49:30,037
Yeah.

865
00:49:30,270 --> 00:49:31,972
Keep an eye out for sharks.

866
00:49:32,406 --> 00:49:35,677
Don't worry about it.
Just keep moving.

867
00:49:35,677 --> 00:49:37,812
Easier said than done, Ray.

868
00:49:38,111 --> 00:49:39,146
Can't count the number
of them bastards

869
00:49:39,413 --> 00:49:41,348
I've caught
over the years.

870
00:49:41,583 --> 00:49:42,684
Kind of unnerving.

871
00:49:44,184 --> 00:49:46,253
We're almost there.

872
00:49:51,124 --> 00:49:53,728
Ray?
Where's the marina?

873
00:49:55,062 --> 00:49:57,097
The storm submerged
all the boats.

874
00:49:58,332 --> 00:50:02,504
This storm, it got bigger
than it was supposed to be.

875
00:50:03,437 --> 00:50:04,939
Bigger than anything
that's hit this town.

876
00:50:05,239 --> 00:50:06,306
And it ain't done yet.

877
00:50:06,574 --> 00:50:07,842
Is there another boat
that we can grab?

878
00:50:08,141 --> 00:50:10,612
No. All the boats
were in the marina.

879
00:50:10,845 --> 00:50:13,080
There's nothing left.

880
00:50:20,020 --> 00:50:22,456
-Aeden!
-Aeden!

881
00:50:22,690 --> 00:50:25,125
Aeden!

882
00:50:25,994 --> 00:50:29,463
-Aeden!
-Aeden!

883
00:50:29,697 --> 00:50:30,598
I got you.

884
00:50:31,533 --> 00:50:36,571
Aeden, Aeden.
It's okay. You're okay.

885
00:50:38,006 --> 00:50:39,339
Brooke, you good?

886
00:50:39,607 --> 00:50:42,510
-Okay?
-I got him. Calm down.

887
00:50:42,744 --> 00:50:45,780
Okay, you're good.

888
00:50:48,048 --> 00:50:49,984
Look!

889
00:50:50,217 --> 00:50:54,622
Hey! Get in that raft
before the sharks get us!

890
00:50:54,923 --> 00:50:57,525
Keep swimming!

891
00:50:58,258 --> 00:51:00,662
You got it, honey.

892
00:51:04,331 --> 00:51:06,099
-Come on.
-Come on!

893
00:51:06,333 --> 00:51:08,803
-Okay. Give me your hand.
-Let's go. Come on.

894
00:51:08,803 --> 00:51:11,739
Come on!

895
00:51:11,973 --> 00:51:13,140
You got it.

896
00:51:13,975 --> 00:51:16,744
Aeden, you're next.
Let's go.

897
00:51:23,585 --> 00:51:26,286
Got room for one more?
Okay.

898
00:51:27,655 --> 00:51:28,523
-Ray!
-Ray!

899
00:51:28,756 --> 00:51:29,289
Are you gonna get in?

900
00:51:29,591 --> 00:51:32,125
I am not getting in that boat.

901
00:51:32,927 --> 00:51:34,161
What do we do now?

902
00:51:34,428 --> 00:51:35,930
I used up my one idea.

903
00:51:36,163 --> 00:51:38,131
And it was a pretty bad one.

904
00:51:38,700 --> 00:51:40,100
-Natasha?
-Okay.

905
00:51:40,334 --> 00:51:43,771
So, we can try Silky's.
It's the boat that I work at.

906
00:51:44,072 --> 00:51:46,106
It's not too far from here.

907
00:51:46,106 --> 00:51:48,408
And it's on higher ground.

908
00:51:48,676 --> 00:51:52,346
Faith, the owner says
that it can survive

909
00:51:52,346 --> 00:51:53,748
Biblical flooding
because it's built so

910
00:51:54,082 --> 00:51:56,084
close to the beach and I could
really go for a shot right now.

911
00:51:56,084 --> 00:51:57,585
Oh yeah.

912
00:51:57,885 --> 00:51:59,721
Tasha's right. If it survives,
that's going to be

913
00:51:59,954 --> 00:52:02,489
the best place to be for
when the Coast Guard comes.

914
00:52:02,724 --> 00:52:04,458
And we've got to
get some shelter.

915
00:52:04,826 --> 00:52:06,861
The worst of the storms
will be hitting

916
00:52:07,095 --> 00:52:08,663
along with that second surge.

917
00:52:08,896 --> 00:52:11,032
I think Silky's is probably
the sturdiest building

918
00:52:11,331 --> 00:52:14,368
around other than the
Manis Beach Lighthouse.

919
00:52:14,602 --> 00:52:15,970
That lighthouse is too far away.

920
00:52:16,236 --> 00:52:17,237
It's a long shot.

921
00:52:17,237 --> 00:52:18,338
If I had to put
money on anything

922
00:52:18,706 --> 00:52:21,408
that's still standing,
it'd be Silky's.

923
00:52:21,408 --> 00:52:22,744
Okay, but I'm not going anywhere

924
00:52:23,011 --> 00:52:24,211
without rescuing
my wife or my son.

925
00:52:24,478 --> 00:52:25,980
We're not going anywhere
without Mom and Logan!

926
00:52:26,213 --> 00:52:27,280
No, we can't let them down.

927
00:52:27,515 --> 00:52:29,449
Hey, you've got
to save yourself

928
00:52:29,684 --> 00:52:31,318
before you can save anyone else.

929
00:52:31,552 --> 00:52:33,988
Okay, we're going
to regroup at Silky's

930
00:52:34,221 --> 00:52:36,057
and we will come
up with a new plan.

931
00:52:36,289 --> 00:52:36,991
-All right?
-Okay, don't worry.

932
00:52:37,324 --> 00:52:38,993
First round of drinks on me.

933
00:52:39,326 --> 00:52:41,729
Paddle, paddle.

934
00:52:48,201 --> 00:52:50,638
Come on.

935
00:52:54,042 --> 00:52:55,843
Dennis, you knucklehead.

936
00:52:57,545 --> 00:53:00,280
He knew to be more careful.
He was a...

937
00:53:00,815 --> 00:53:02,282
He was not a rookie.

938
00:53:09,691 --> 00:53:10,725
My name's Faith.

939
00:53:11,159 --> 00:53:12,627
This is my establishment.

940
00:53:14,796 --> 00:53:16,931
Locals.

941
00:53:18,633 --> 00:53:20,802
Stephen...

942
00:53:22,235 --> 00:53:24,304
Mary...

943
00:53:24,605 --> 00:53:27,374
Noah.

944
00:53:32,914 --> 00:53:34,481
I'm Sarah.

945
00:53:34,716 --> 00:53:35,717
This is Logan.

946
00:53:40,188 --> 00:53:44,125
Silky's has stood
straight since 1966.

947
00:53:44,357 --> 00:53:46,861
And no salt water has
ever gotten on my floor.

948
00:53:48,361 --> 00:53:49,697
You're safe here.

949
00:53:49,697 --> 00:53:51,566
No, we're not!

950
00:53:53,300 --> 00:53:56,804
Listen, a shark got
in our house.

951
00:53:57,105 --> 00:53:59,540
This town is a fishbowl.

952
00:54:00,641 --> 00:54:02,076
The reason that we have survived

953
00:54:02,342 --> 00:54:05,479
is we are above
the flood level, okay?

954
00:54:06,547 --> 00:54:10,718
He's seen someone he knows
get killed today.

955
00:54:12,920 --> 00:54:16,958
I thinks it's safe to say that
we've all lost someone tonight.

956
00:54:21,596 --> 00:54:25,032
I don't even know where
his sister or my husband are.

957
00:54:26,134 --> 00:54:29,436
And... Mae did not deserve...

958
00:54:29,737 --> 00:54:30,872
Mae?

959
00:54:31,139 --> 00:54:33,941
Mae Baldwin?

960
00:54:34,909 --> 00:54:37,377
Is she...

961
00:54:38,411 --> 00:54:40,848
Yeah.

962
00:54:42,717 --> 00:54:45,253
I'm really sorry to hear that.

963
00:54:45,452 --> 00:54:46,921
She's, um...

964
00:54:47,221 --> 00:54:48,556
She was a good person.

965
00:54:52,560 --> 00:54:54,929
So how do we plan on
getting out of all of this?

966
00:54:58,132 --> 00:54:59,901
We sit and wait.

967
00:55:00,467 --> 00:55:04,371
For the water to go away
and the cavalry to show up.

968
00:55:06,306 --> 00:55:08,042
Anything else is just too risky.

969
00:55:08,441 --> 00:55:11,078
Those sharks.

970
00:55:16,284 --> 00:55:18,619
Faith?

971
00:55:19,120 --> 00:55:22,489
This building isn't
gonna fall apart, is it?

972
00:55:26,227 --> 00:55:27,295
There's no guarantee
on anything,

973
00:55:27,460 --> 00:55:29,597
but I think she'll hold.

974
00:55:30,765 --> 00:55:33,034
Been through a lot.
She's still standing.

975
00:55:34,969 --> 00:55:37,370
Hey.

976
00:55:38,940 --> 00:55:45,112
You have seen things today that
nobody should have to see, okay?

977
00:55:45,412 --> 00:55:47,615
And I'm really sorry about that.

978
00:55:48,616 --> 00:55:50,718
But I'm going to...
Look at me. Look at me.

979
00:55:51,018 --> 00:55:54,255
I'm going to make sure that
we get out of here, okay?

980
00:55:54,255 --> 00:55:56,356
Okay, come here.

981
00:55:58,559 --> 00:56:00,127
It's okay.
I love you.

982
00:56:01,562 --> 00:56:02,830
I love you.

983
00:56:12,607 --> 00:56:15,910
Woo! Look!
It's still standing!

984
00:56:16,210 --> 00:56:18,813
Thank God.

985
00:56:21,115 --> 00:56:23,818
I want to thank you for
keeping Brooke safe tonight.

986
00:56:24,451 --> 00:56:26,854
We kept each other safe.

987
00:56:27,088 --> 00:56:28,990
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have
been at the beach this morning.

988
00:56:29,290 --> 00:56:30,758
It's okay.

989
00:56:30,992 --> 00:56:31,626
Okay, baby?

990
00:56:31,626 --> 00:56:32,927
Paddle, everybody!

991
00:56:32,927 --> 00:56:34,394
This boat is taking
on a lot of water.

992
00:56:34,829 --> 00:56:36,564
I don't know if it's gonna
stay afloat until we get there.

993
00:56:36,564 --> 00:56:37,732
Oh, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no!

994
00:56:37,965 --> 00:56:40,433
We're caught!

995
00:56:40,668 --> 00:56:44,071
Let's go! Paddle!
Paddle faster!

996
00:56:44,639 --> 00:56:47,909
Come on! Come on!

997
00:56:48,276 --> 00:56:51,444
Boilermakers.

998
00:56:51,679 --> 00:56:53,748
This was Denni' favorite drink.

999
00:56:55,016 --> 00:56:55,917
Boilermakers.

1000
00:56:56,150 --> 00:56:57,417
He did not care what kind of

1001
00:56:57,618 --> 00:57:00,154
whiskey I gave him,
what kind of beer.

1002
00:57:00,755 --> 00:57:02,189
This was his drink.

1003
00:57:05,159 --> 00:57:08,162
I remember one night,

1004
00:57:08,396 --> 00:57:10,064
a bunch of college kids came in,

1005
00:57:10,064 --> 00:57:12,733
hooting and hollering.

1006
00:57:13,100 --> 00:57:15,903
But... Dennis hated it
when the younger crowd hated it.

1007
00:57:15,903 --> 00:57:17,605
Bartenders loved it,
because that's the only time

1008
00:57:17,838 --> 00:57:19,507
they could actually
make some money.

1009
00:57:19,974 --> 00:57:23,476
Not like the 50-cent tips
Dennis would give them.

1010
00:57:33,688 --> 00:57:36,657
The college kids
started doing shots.

1011
00:57:37,425 --> 00:57:39,193
So Dennis challenged them to see

1012
00:57:39,393 --> 00:57:41,162
who could do the
most Boilermakers.

1013
00:57:42,663 --> 00:57:44,298
They had no idea
what it even was.

1014
00:57:44,565 --> 00:57:45,533
But they were game.

1015
00:57:45,800 --> 00:57:48,069
So he let them choose
the whiskey,

1016
00:57:48,369 --> 00:57:49,737
let them choose the beer.

1017
00:57:50,504 --> 00:57:52,773
I was serious when
I said he did not care.

1018
00:57:53,574 --> 00:57:55,710
I watched them do

1019
00:57:56,243 --> 00:58:01,215
one, two, three, four down.

1020
00:58:01,515 --> 00:58:03,217
Nobody even seemed fazed.

1021
00:58:04,685 --> 00:58:08,222
He really got those
college kids, huh?

1022
00:58:08,488 --> 00:58:11,993
No.
They drank him under the table.

1023
00:58:14,528 --> 00:58:16,564
Dennis fell asleep with
his head on the bar

1024
00:58:16,797 --> 00:58:18,532
until after the close.

1025
00:58:25,639 --> 00:58:28,809
I am going to miss
that knucklehead.

1026
00:58:31,045 --> 00:58:33,614
Coral Bay is not going
to be the same after this.

1027
00:58:38,652 --> 00:58:40,888
-To Dennis.
-Dennis!

1028
00:58:47,628 --> 00:58:52,600
Go! Climb the ladder!
Let's go! Go! Come on!

1029
00:58:59,940 --> 00:59:00,908
Brooke!

1030
00:59:01,242 --> 00:59:03,844
Okay, got you!
Come on.

1031
00:59:04,045 --> 00:59:07,715
Go, Aeden.
Come on. You got this.

1032
00:59:07,948 --> 00:59:10,017
You can do it, buddy.
That's it.

1033
00:59:10,251 --> 00:59:13,154
Okay.
Good job.

1034
00:59:15,456 --> 00:59:16,924
There's a door over there!

1035
00:59:17,158 --> 00:59:18,159
I got you!

1036
00:59:24,065 --> 00:59:26,600
Come on, Ray.

1037
00:59:27,568 --> 00:59:29,236
Silky's still standing!

1038
00:59:33,107 --> 00:59:37,311
-Sarah? Sarah, we're here!
-Faith! Faith!

1039
00:59:37,678 --> 00:59:39,548
-Brooke!
-Mom!

1040
00:59:39,780 --> 00:59:43,017
Oh my God! Logan!

1041
00:59:45,086 --> 00:59:45,419
Hey, it's okay.

1042
00:59:45,786 --> 00:59:48,355
It's okay, it's okay.

1043
01:00:01,735 --> 01:00:04,438
How bad is it?

1044
01:00:05,172 --> 01:00:06,740
This is the worst
I've ever seen

1045
01:00:06,740 --> 01:00:08,577
and it's only
getting uglier.

1046
01:00:08,943 --> 01:00:09,610
It's not letting up.

1047
01:00:09,610 --> 01:00:11,078
What's the town?

1048
01:00:11,879 --> 01:00:15,149
It's, uh, it's underwater.
It's crazy.

1049
01:00:15,584 --> 01:00:16,784
Good God.

1050
01:00:16,784 --> 01:00:19,353
Oh, God.
I'm so sorry.

1051
01:00:21,188 --> 01:00:23,624
Where's my mother?

1052
01:00:29,296 --> 01:00:30,831
Is she here?

1053
01:00:31,866 --> 01:00:34,502
Did she come with you guys?

1054
01:00:34,502 --> 01:00:36,237
Is she still at home?

1055
01:00:42,710 --> 01:00:44,044
What?

1056
01:00:44,345 --> 01:00:45,846
What is it?

1057
01:00:46,780 --> 01:00:47,815
What?

1058
01:00:48,048 --> 01:00:49,650
Honey...

1059
01:00:49,950 --> 01:00:51,085
Why are you crying?

1060
01:00:51,085 --> 01:00:54,388
-I'm so sorry.
-No... No.

1061
01:00:54,556 --> 01:00:57,224
No!

1062
01:00:57,458 --> 01:00:58,560
I'm so sorry.

1063
01:00:58,859 --> 01:01:01,428
No... No...

1064
01:01:06,267 --> 01:01:08,702
He lost both of
his parents tonight.

1065
01:01:32,126 --> 01:01:36,363
Aeden, if you need anything,
we're all here for you, okay?

1066
01:01:50,579 --> 01:01:51,779
Ray.

1067
01:01:52,046 --> 01:01:52,713
I want to introduce
you to my family.

1068
01:01:52,713 --> 01:01:53,447
This is...

1069
01:01:53,714 --> 01:01:55,182
This is my wife, Sarah.

1070
01:01:55,482 --> 01:01:57,552
And my son, Logan.

1071
01:01:57,552 --> 01:01:59,386
They saved us out there tonight.

1072
01:02:04,626 --> 01:02:06,060
Thank you so much.

1073
01:02:06,595 --> 01:02:07,629
Just pay the favor forward.

1074
01:02:07,861 --> 01:02:09,964
I'll be forever grateful for
you.

1075
01:02:11,799 --> 01:02:13,635
Hey, you guys.

1076
01:02:13,934 --> 01:02:16,203
All Silky's has to do
is get us through this

1077
01:02:16,437 --> 01:02:18,372
second surge and the
strongest part of the storm,

1078
01:02:18,372 --> 01:02:21,208
and we're going to
be over this nightmare.

1079
01:02:24,812 --> 01:02:28,182
[screams]

1080
01:02:30,251 --> 01:02:32,253
Faith, no!

1081
01:02:32,520 --> 01:02:33,487
Go, go, go!

1082
01:02:33,722 --> 01:02:35,557
Go to the roof!
Go to the roof! Go!

1083
01:02:35,789 --> 01:02:37,091
Go to the roof!

1084
01:02:38,627 --> 01:02:40,494
Tasha! Come on!
Let's go!

1085
01:02:40,761 --> 01:02:42,830
Move, move!
No! No! I won't!

1086
01:02:43,130 --> 01:02:45,833
He saved me!
He's all I got left!

1087
01:02:46,133 --> 01:02:47,569
Then I can't leave him, either.

1088
01:02:47,801 --> 01:02:50,304
Come on, your family needs you.
Go! Go!

1089
01:02:50,605 --> 01:02:53,240
Go! Both of you!

1090
01:02:54,208 --> 01:02:56,210
Come on, you son of a bitch.

1091
01:02:57,411 --> 01:02:59,947
No!

1092
01:03:00,247 --> 01:03:01,348
Ray!

1093
01:03:01,583 --> 01:03:05,152
No!

1094
01:03:14,194 --> 01:03:16,631
Is everyone here?
Is everyone okay?

1095
01:03:16,864 --> 01:03:17,766
Yeah, the kids are here.

1096
01:03:17,998 --> 01:03:20,401
You feeling okay?

1097
01:03:20,735 --> 01:03:22,537
Tasha? Where's Ray?

1098
01:03:22,870 --> 01:03:25,205
He's gone!
He's gone!

1099
01:03:26,574 --> 01:03:28,242
Are we safe up here?

1100
01:03:28,543 --> 01:03:29,310
No.

1101
01:03:29,544 --> 01:03:31,178
Nowhere is safe.

1102
01:03:31,478 --> 01:03:33,113
No! Nowhere is safe!

1103
01:03:33,447 --> 01:03:36,785
Okay, this building is not
going to stand for much longer.

1104
01:03:37,017 --> 01:03:39,887
And if the storm is too
much for Silky's...

1105
01:03:40,120 --> 01:03:43,090
Then we need to
figure something out.

1106
01:03:43,957 --> 01:03:46,260
And if that completely
breaks loose...

1107
01:03:53,934 --> 01:03:55,469
There!
We need to get there.

1108
01:03:55,770 --> 01:03:59,173
Right!

1109
01:04:00,407 --> 01:04:02,910
That is a bit of a swim in
shark-infested waters, guys.

1110
01:04:02,910 --> 01:04:03,944
Well, one way or another,

1111
01:04:04,311 --> 01:04:06,781
we're going to end up
back in that water.

1112
01:04:07,014 --> 01:04:08,817
And tha's the only place I see.

1113
01:04:09,016 --> 01:04:10,685
Unlike all these buildings,
it shouldn't fall apart.

1114
01:04:10,984 --> 01:04:14,254
Okay. There.
There's no live wires.

1115
01:04:15,122 --> 01:04:16,390
The water is so cold,
we have to try to find

1116
01:04:16,691 --> 01:04:18,492
a way to stay out of it
for as long as we can

1117
01:04:18,727 --> 01:04:20,662
or we're going
to all risk getting hypothermia

1118
01:04:20,894 --> 01:04:22,162
on top of everything else.

1119
01:04:22,396 --> 01:04:24,599
Another thing to
add to the list, right?

1120
01:04:24,932 --> 01:04:25,933
Look, in just a little bit,

1121
01:04:26,266 --> 01:04:28,235
we can drive right
out of this basin,

1122
01:04:28,235 --> 01:04:31,539
away from these sharks,
and get out of this water, okay?

1123
01:04:31,539 --> 01:04:34,942
Okay? We've just got to
find a way to get to it.

1124
01:04:35,175 --> 01:04:37,211
Maybe more debris?

1125
01:04:41,783 --> 01:04:42,916
Sounds like we got to go now.

1126
01:04:43,217 --> 01:04:45,185
All right! Right now
before we get electrocuted!

1127
01:04:45,419 --> 01:04:48,021
Okay, I'm gonna go first
and help everyone else down.

1128
01:04:48,222 --> 01:04:51,726
Let's go!
Go! Go! Hurry up!

1129
01:04:51,992 --> 01:04:53,795
Okay, we have no choice.

1130
01:04:54,027 --> 01:04:55,864
We've just got to
jump and swim for it!

1131
01:04:55,864 --> 01:04:58,198
Okay! I'm going in!

1132
01:05:09,577 --> 01:05:10,578
Come on!

1133
01:05:10,812 --> 01:05:13,247
Brooke, Aeden, let's go!

1134
01:05:28,897 --> 01:05:31,766
Aeden! Are you okay?

1135
01:05:32,099 --> 01:05:34,501
My leg.
It's cramping again.

1136
01:05:40,742 --> 01:05:42,376
You guys ready?

1137
01:05:43,511 --> 01:05:46,079
No!

1138
01:05:53,922 --> 01:05:55,155
Come on!

1139
01:05:55,389 --> 01:05:56,957
Oh, God.

1140
01:05:57,191 --> 01:06:00,595
Mom, come on.

1141
01:06:01,028 --> 01:06:03,531
[shrieks]

1142
01:06:10,672 --> 01:06:13,508
-Logan!
-Logan!

1143
01:06:17,244 --> 01:06:18,880
I got you!
I got you!

1144
01:06:19,112 --> 01:06:20,047
You okay?

1145
01:06:20,280 --> 01:06:23,484
-No! No!
-Keep moving!

1146
01:06:23,751 --> 01:06:27,020
Get moving!

1147
01:06:36,931 --> 01:06:37,866
Keep swimming.

1148
01:06:38,165 --> 01:06:41,335
I got you, come on.

1149
01:06:42,069 --> 01:06:44,539
Keep swimming.

1150
01:06:45,038 --> 01:06:46,608
You got this.

1151
01:06:46,875 --> 01:06:49,309
I see it.

1152
01:06:51,445 --> 01:06:54,749
-That big truck!
-I see it! Come on!

1153
01:06:55,015 --> 01:06:57,384
We'll get to it.
Keep swimming!

1154
01:06:57,652 --> 01:07:00,420
Come on!
I got you.

1155
01:07:02,590 --> 01:07:04,592
Come on.

1156
01:07:04,826 --> 01:07:08,362
-Tasha, Tasha!
-Come on!

1157
01:07:09,396 --> 01:07:12,499
Come on.
Come on, baby.

1158
01:07:12,734 --> 01:07:14,401
You got this.

1159
01:07:14,702 --> 01:07:17,137
Come on, girl.

1160
01:07:22,577 --> 01:07:24,879
Take her!

1161
01:07:25,112 --> 01:07:25,880
You got this?

1162
01:07:26,179 --> 01:07:28,315
Hold on!

1163
01:07:28,850 --> 01:07:31,886
Mark! Mark! There's a shark!
There's sharks!

1164
01:07:32,152 --> 01:07:34,589
Come on!

1165
01:07:38,058 --> 01:07:41,596
Mark, you gotta
get out of the water!

1166
01:07:45,600 --> 01:07:46,534
Got it?

1167
01:07:46,768 --> 01:07:49,236
-All right, everybody inside!
-All right.

1168
01:07:49,537 --> 01:07:52,674
Okay, it's empty.
Come on!

1169
01:07:52,941 --> 01:07:55,309
Get in the back!

1170
01:08:02,517 --> 01:08:04,251
Let's get this thing started.

1171
01:08:04,552 --> 01:08:07,055
We can drive to higher ground.

1172
01:08:07,321 --> 01:08:08,790
-I got it.
-You got the keys?

1173
01:08:09,089 --> 01:08:11,458
All right.

1174
01:08:12,026 --> 01:08:13,661
[engine sputters]

1175
01:08:13,895 --> 01:08:15,295
Damn it!

1176
01:08:15,530 --> 01:08:16,064
Try again.

1177
01:08:16,330 --> 01:08:19,399
Come on, come on.

1178
01:08:20,735 --> 01:08:22,102
Damn it!

1179
01:08:22,102 --> 01:08:22,904
Okay.

1180
01:08:23,203 --> 01:08:25,607
Okay, don't worry, okay?

1181
01:08:26,173 --> 01:08:27,942
Because this thing's
on top of the hill,

1182
01:08:28,241 --> 01:08:30,745
we should be able to
ride out the second surge.

1183
01:08:31,445 --> 01:08:32,714
We'll ride it out in here.

1184
01:08:33,014 --> 01:08:35,415
Together.

1185
01:08:35,783 --> 01:08:36,818
As a family.

1186
01:08:37,752 --> 01:08:38,620
Okay, all right.

1187
01:08:38,820 --> 01:08:40,021
Let's go.

1188
01:08:40,253 --> 01:08:41,488
We're safer back here.

1189
01:08:41,789 --> 01:08:44,124
Come on.

1190
01:08:53,300 --> 01:08:55,603
Aeden, are you okay?

1191
01:08:55,837 --> 01:08:58,171
Not really.

1192
01:09:00,508 --> 01:09:01,776
Hey.

1193
01:09:02,076 --> 01:09:03,945
Promise me you'll
hold it together,

1194
01:09:03,945 --> 01:09:06,748
and I promise you that
I will get us out of here.

1195
01:09:07,015 --> 01:09:08,482
Okay?

1196
01:09:08,683 --> 01:09:10,852
I know that you've
had a hell of a night,

1197
01:09:11,085 --> 01:09:13,121
and that truck wouldn't start,

1198
01:09:13,320 --> 01:09:16,256
but someone will
eventually come for us.

1199
01:09:16,557 --> 01:09:18,760
Okay?

1200
01:09:24,766 --> 01:09:26,534
In the meantime,
why don't we try to

1201
01:09:26,734 --> 01:09:29,570
look out for another
vehicle or any other

1202
01:09:29,804 --> 01:09:31,238
buildings that, uh,

1203
01:09:31,572 --> 01:09:33,875
that won't be compromised,
just in case...

1204
01:09:34,174 --> 01:09:36,911
Mark...
Mark, no.

1205
01:09:37,210 --> 01:09:38,680
There is nothing else.

1206
01:09:39,446 --> 01:09:41,281
If Silky's couldn't
stand the storm,

1207
01:09:41,281 --> 01:09:44,284
then there are no
buildings standing.

1208
01:09:44,819 --> 01:09:46,587
The thing was
built like a bunker.

1209
01:09:46,921 --> 01:09:49,691
No, what about the
lighthouse that Ray mentioned?

1210
01:09:49,891 --> 01:09:52,927
It's ancient, okay?

1211
01:09:53,193 --> 01:09:55,362
Even if it survived
the first surge,

1212
01:09:55,663 --> 01:09:58,432
it's not going to survive
the second time.

1213
01:10:01,569 --> 01:10:05,272
I'm sorry about all this.

1214
01:10:05,472 --> 01:10:10,511
I'm sorry about the stress
that I caused by losing my job.

1215
01:10:10,745 --> 01:10:13,715
I'm sorry that I thought
a vacation would help us.

1216
01:10:15,116 --> 01:10:18,853
No, it feels so silly now.

1217
01:10:21,455 --> 01:10:22,890
It all feels so silly now.

1218
01:10:23,124 --> 01:10:24,959
I'm just...

1219
01:10:25,325 --> 01:10:27,562
I'm just glad that
we're all together.

1220
01:10:28,563 --> 01:10:30,230
And we're all still alive.

1221
01:10:32,800 --> 01:10:33,835
I love you.

1222
01:10:39,473 --> 01:10:42,143
Why doesn't anyone
come to rescue us?

1223
01:10:42,375 --> 01:10:43,878
It's not safe.

1224
01:10:47,815 --> 01:10:51,753
Not until that
second surge is over.

1225
01:10:51,986 --> 01:10:54,088
Isn't it like people's jobs
or something

1226
01:10:54,287 --> 01:10:55,890
to go into
dangerous places?

1227
01:10:56,157 --> 01:10:59,861
Buddy, as a paramedic, our core
principle is scene safety.

1228
01:11:00,194 --> 01:11:01,562
Which means you can't
rescue anyone

1229
01:11:01,896 --> 01:11:04,031
if you're killed
or injured first.

1230
01:11:05,298 --> 01:11:09,737
As long as that second surge
doesn't hit us, we'll be okay.

1231
01:11:10,337 --> 01:11:12,006
We just have to
hold on a couple more hours

1232
01:11:12,240 --> 01:11:15,610
until the water recedes and
then someone will come for us.

1233
01:11:16,210 --> 01:11:18,746
More hours?

1234
01:11:23,350 --> 01:11:25,418
Um...

1235
01:11:25,653 --> 01:11:28,556
Was my mom mad at
me when you last saw her?

1236
01:11:29,924 --> 01:11:31,526
No, honey.

1237
01:11:31,759 --> 01:11:34,061
Honey, listen to me.
She was not mad.

1238
01:11:34,361 --> 01:11:36,631
She was just worried.

1239
01:11:36,931 --> 01:11:39,366
I just... I just don't want
her last thoughts

1240
01:11:39,667 --> 01:11:42,302
to have been, like,
angry ones.

1241
01:11:46,339 --> 01:11:47,909
I just want to go home.

1242
01:11:48,276 --> 01:11:50,878
We will go home
eventually, buddy, okay?

1243
01:11:51,112 --> 01:11:52,513
I promise you.

1244
01:11:53,848 --> 01:11:55,348
I promise you.

1245
01:12:07,528 --> 01:12:08,495
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Okay, okay.

1246
01:12:09,030 --> 01:12:11,799
Well, we gotta go now
because it's flooding, guys.

1247
01:12:14,001 --> 01:12:14,869
Come on, let's go!

1248
01:12:14,869 --> 01:12:15,736
Dad!

1249
01:12:16,003 --> 01:12:17,305
No, no, okay.
It's gonna be okay.

1250
01:12:17,538 --> 01:12:18,739
You know what?

1251
01:12:18,973 --> 01:12:20,875
When the water recedes,
the boats and helicopters,

1252
01:12:21,108 --> 01:12:22,475
they'll be able to see
us better from up here.

1253
01:12:22,475 --> 01:12:23,410
We're gonna go.
We're gonna be okay.

1254
01:12:23,678 --> 01:12:25,646
All right, kids first!
Let's go!

1255
01:12:26,413 --> 01:12:28,381
Let's go! Hurry!

1256
01:12:28,616 --> 01:12:30,417
-We're gonna be okay.
-Let's go!

1257
01:12:30,618 --> 01:12:33,988
Come on.
Come on, one at a time.

1258
01:12:36,057 --> 01:12:36,958
Hurry!

1259
01:12:37,191 --> 01:12:39,861
I'm trying!

1260
01:12:56,110 --> 01:12:59,213
-Aeden!
-Ow!

1261
01:12:59,479 --> 01:13:01,949
Aeden!

1262
01:13:03,551 --> 01:13:05,686
Brooke!
What happened?

1263
01:13:05,987 --> 01:13:07,221
-Brooke!
-Brooke!

1264
01:13:07,487 --> 01:13:09,090
Aeden!

1265
01:13:09,389 --> 01:13:10,390
Mark, the kids are in the water!

1266
01:13:10,390 --> 01:13:12,026
I got it!
Hang on!

1267
01:13:18,498 --> 01:13:22,536
Come on!
I gotta get Brooke. Go!

1268
01:13:24,138 --> 01:13:25,072
Mark, hurry!

1269
01:13:25,306 --> 01:13:26,607
Come on, honey!

1270
01:13:29,010 --> 01:13:31,846
I'm stuck!

1271
01:13:36,284 --> 01:13:37,385
What? Where is she?

1272
01:13:37,618 --> 01:13:39,987
She's stuck!

1273
01:13:42,757 --> 01:13:44,592
I can't get her up!

1274
01:13:44,859 --> 01:13:47,862
Come on, try to
get out of there!

1275
01:13:48,095 --> 01:13:50,898
It's not a shark, is it?

1276
01:13:54,035 --> 01:13:54,602
Where are they?

1277
01:13:54,869 --> 01:13:56,938
Mark, I'm coming to help!

1278
01:13:57,171 --> 01:13:59,974
No, Tasha!

1279
01:14:01,609 --> 01:14:02,710
Come on, you gotta move!

1280
01:14:02,944 --> 01:14:05,179
There's at least three
coming right at you!

1281
01:14:05,546 --> 01:14:07,048
Mark!

1282
01:14:07,315 --> 01:14:08,983
Come on! Come on!

1283
01:14:09,550 --> 01:14:12,019
Give me your hand!

1284
01:14:17,490 --> 01:14:19,193
-Swim!
-I'm trying!

1285
01:14:19,527 --> 01:14:21,896
Swim, Brooke!

1286
01:14:23,931 --> 01:14:26,767
Mark! Mark!

1287
01:14:33,240 --> 01:14:36,476
You got her?
You good?

1288
01:14:38,612 --> 01:14:39,747
I got you!

1289
01:14:40,081 --> 01:14:42,316
Mark, come back!

1290
01:14:42,616 --> 01:14:44,785
Come on, Mark,
get back in here!

1291
01:14:45,586 --> 01:14:47,121
Come on, let her go!

1292
01:14:47,722 --> 01:14:49,557
There are three sharks
coming right at you!

1293
01:14:49,890 --> 01:14:52,159
-Faster!
-Come on, hurry up!

1294
01:14:57,497 --> 01:14:59,100
-Tasha!
-No!

1295
01:14:59,367 --> 01:15:01,936
-I gotta go get her!
-No, no, no!

1296
01:15:03,704 --> 01:15:04,572
I gotta go get her!

1297
01:15:04,772 --> 01:15:08,843
-Honey, stop!
-Tasha!

1298
01:15:14,382 --> 01:15:19,253
No! It's too late!
I'm so sorry!

1299
01:15:20,821 --> 01:15:23,591
I think we're moving!
I think we're floating!

1300
01:15:23,858 --> 01:15:25,226
The second surge is hitting!

1301
01:15:25,459 --> 01:15:27,862
Hang on!

1302
01:15:31,599 --> 01:15:32,666
It's on fire!

1303
01:15:32,900 --> 01:15:34,502
The transformer blew!

1304
01:15:34,802 --> 01:15:37,138
We have to get off of
here before we get hit!

1305
01:15:37,738 --> 01:15:39,607
We have to jump, guys!
We have no choice!

1306
01:15:39,840 --> 01:15:41,876
Ready?
On the count of three!

1307
01:15:42,109 --> 01:15:46,213
One! Two! Three!

1308
01:15:57,425 --> 01:15:58,459
Are you guys good?

1309
01:15:58,692 --> 01:16:01,262
Everyone okay?

1310
01:16:05,800 --> 01:16:08,869
Try to keep moving!
Conserve your energy!

1311
01:16:10,805 --> 01:16:14,241
Brooke! Brooke!

1312
01:16:15,643 --> 01:16:17,078
Hey, hey, hey!

1313
01:16:17,344 --> 01:16:18,579
You need to breathe, okay?

1314
01:16:18,813 --> 01:16:21,115
You need to stay conscious.

1315
01:16:21,415 --> 01:16:23,217
You're going into shock.

1316
01:16:23,518 --> 01:16:24,952
Okay, listen to me.
Listen to me.

1317
01:16:25,219 --> 01:16:26,854
When it's high tide...

1318
01:16:27,188 --> 01:16:28,889
-No!
-No!

1319
01:16:29,190 --> 01:16:31,659
Things will hopefully
get better, okay?

1320
01:16:31,926 --> 01:16:33,194
Just keep moving.

1321
01:16:34,695 --> 01:16:36,597
Help will eventually come.

1322
01:16:36,831 --> 01:16:38,799
Do you hear that?

1323
01:16:39,100 --> 01:16:41,570
I think it's a helicopter!
I think it's a helicopter!

1324
01:16:41,802 --> 01:16:44,305
What are you
talking about, Logan?

1325
01:16:44,539 --> 01:16:46,674
Did you see that?
Did you see that?

1326
01:16:46,974 --> 01:16:48,642
It was right there!

1327
01:16:49,376 --> 01:16:50,678
-Lightning!
-It's okay.

1328
01:16:50,945 --> 01:16:54,715
It's hypothermia.
You need to relax.

1329
01:16:55,517 --> 01:16:57,586
Where'd it go?
Where'd it go?

1330
01:16:57,818 --> 01:17:00,187
Where'd it go?

1331
01:17:00,488 --> 01:17:04,024
It's okay.
It's okay, buddy.

1332
01:17:04,258 --> 01:17:06,961
Hey! We need to get our
body temperatures up.

1333
01:17:07,194 --> 01:17:08,095
Keep moving!

1334
01:17:08,329 --> 01:17:10,131
Come on.

1335
01:17:10,364 --> 01:17:11,632
What is that?

1336
01:17:11,866 --> 01:17:13,234
I see something, too!

1337
01:17:13,602 --> 01:17:17,705
Keep moving.
We got this. We got this.

1338
01:17:18,272 --> 01:17:19,773
It's a lighthouse.

1339
01:17:20,007 --> 01:17:21,709
Manis Beach lighthouse.

1340
01:17:21,976 --> 01:17:24,245
We must have traveled
several miles from downtown.

1341
01:17:24,478 --> 01:17:25,514
It's still standing!

1342
01:17:25,813 --> 01:17:27,181
Okay, we just need
to make it there.

1343
01:17:27,181 --> 01:17:29,416
If we get inside, we can
ride the rest of this out.

1344
01:17:29,717 --> 01:17:32,987
She's withstood
the storm's so far.

1345
01:17:33,220 --> 01:17:34,589
Can we make it?

1346
01:17:34,822 --> 01:17:36,090
We've come this far.
Come on!

1347
01:17:36,090 --> 01:17:37,024
We need to hurry

1348
01:17:37,358 --> 01:17:38,926
before we have to
fight against the tide.

1349
01:17:39,160 --> 01:17:41,795
Go!

1350
01:17:43,831 --> 01:17:46,233
To the lighthouse!
Keep moving!

1351
01:17:47,902 --> 01:17:49,270
Sharks are coming!

1352
01:17:49,670 --> 01:17:52,507
I'm going.
I can't make it.

1353
01:17:52,740 --> 01:17:56,210
Sharks! Sharks!

1354
01:18:04,586 --> 01:18:06,921
Keep going!

1355
01:18:12,426 --> 01:18:14,962
[gasps]

1356
01:18:16,363 --> 01:18:18,799
No!

1357
01:18:53,434 --> 01:18:56,737
[gasping, coughing]

1358
01:19:11,919 --> 01:19:15,155
-Logan...
-What's that?

1359
01:19:17,091 --> 01:19:18,526
-Come on!
-Help me out!

1360
01:19:23,030 --> 01:19:25,099
-Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom!
-Hold her head.

1361
01:19:25,399 --> 01:19:26,701
Oh my God.

1362
01:19:26,934 --> 01:19:29,970
I'm gonna start compressing.
Straighten her feet.

1363
01:19:32,139 --> 01:19:34,341
Mom!

1364
01:19:37,612 --> 01:19:38,846
-Stay with me, Sarah.
-Mom?

1365
01:19:39,113 --> 01:19:40,615
-Come on, baby. Come on.
-Please, open your eyes, Mom.

1366
01:19:40,881 --> 01:19:43,417
Stay with me, Sarah.

1367
01:19:47,154 --> 01:19:51,392
Sarah? Sarah?
Oh, baby! Baby!

1368
01:19:51,626 --> 01:19:54,295
[helicopter approaching]

1369
01:19:58,799 --> 01:20:01,402
Look!

1370
01:20:51,151 --> 01:20:52,920
Over here! Please!